  "description": "T1. Ash\t\r\nRear Communal Area\r\nRemove dead branches over 2.5cm in diameter and small sections of Ivy from the base.\r\nCarry out a climbing inspection to ascertain the general condition and report adverse findings.\r\nThe tree's current height is 19m, and its crown spread is 11m.\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 19m and the crown spread is 11m. \r\n\r\nT3. Ash x 3\t\r\nRear Communal Area\r\nGroup of 3 Ash trees, reduce the height of the tallest tree by 3m or to the previous pruning points, reduce lateral spread by 1.5m to balance. - Carry out a climbing inspection on the front two Ash trees and remove any dead wood over 2.5cm in diameter.\r\nWe would suggest the removal or relocation of the compost area in the centre of three Ash trees, as this may affect the trees' root systems. (3rd party or gardener to carry out these works).\r\nThe tree's current average tree height in the group is 16m, and its crown spread is 12m.\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 13m and the crown spread is 11m. \r\n\r\nT4. Ash\t\r\nFront Drive Area:\r\nPoor in general health.\r\nInonotus hispidus fungal bracket is present on the main stem.\r\nLarge cavity at 1-1.5m.\r\nReduce regrowth in height by 3m or back to the previous points.\r\nThe tree's current height is 12m, and its crown spread is 5m\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 11m and the crown spread is 5m \r\n\r\nT5. Birch\t\r\nRear Communal Area\r\nRemove dead branches over 2.5cm in diameter only.\r\nPossible ground heave and movement to the adjacent fence.\r\nCarry out a stability test to ascertain root plate movement.The tree's current height is 14m, and its crown spread is 6m.\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 14m and the crown spread is 6m.",
